mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>z</mi></mtd><mtd><mi></mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>2</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></li>\n</ul>\n<div id=\"graphic-q-156118-e-1\" class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/q-156118-e-1\"></div>\n\n<p>To find the values of <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"78\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D467 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>z</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> that satisfy both inequalities, we find where the two solutions overlap:</p>\n<div id=\"graphic-q-156118-e-2\" class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/q-156118-e-2\"></div>\n\n<p>It turns out that the solutions do not overlap at all. Therefore, there are no values of <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"79\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D467 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>z</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> that satisfy both inequalities simultaneously. So, there is no solution.</p>\n</div></div>",
